%% CANARY for the opt-out: a marker naming a rule this guard cannot emit.
%% A typo, a rule renamed since the marker was written, or a rule invented by an author who assumed
%% one existed. All three suppress NOTHING while reading exactly like a working exemption, which is
%% strictly worse than no marker: the next reader sees an exception where there is none.
%% EXPECT: optout-unknown-rule | blind OPTOUT_RE — blind the marker pattern and the line reverts to
%% an ordinary mermaid comment, taking the finding with it. That is the only thing keeping it alive:
%% the diagram below is clean, so nothing else in this file can produce a finding of any kind.
flowchart TB
%% MUST-FIRE
%% diagram-size-ok: tall-labl — typo'd rule name; this excuses nothing at all
  a["one line"] --> b["also one line"]
